R"VG(
# modern5.vg (H-04, the second pass): the modern age's reports (a ministry's, a board's, a company's: the figures, a survey, the
# recommendation nobody follows). Every sentence is built from parts, the people's own crops, crafts, waters and quarters in the figures,
# each people's inspectors with their own few ways of recommending and closing (`people=K`). The scientific paper is modern9.vg's.

genre.mreport (words=23..90)
  {mr.head}\n{mr.summary}\n{mr.finding} {mr.finding}\n{mr.rec}
  {mr.head}\n{mr.summary}\n{mr.finding} {mr.finding} {mr.finding}\n{mr.rec}
  {mr.head}\n{mr.finding} {mr.survey}\n{mr.rec} {mr.coda}
  {mr.head}\n{mr.summary}\n{mr.compare} {mr.finding}\n{mr.rec}
  {mr.head}\n{mr.survey} {mr.finding}\n{mr.rec} {mr.coda}

mr.head (formula people=3)
  Report to {ruler.the}, {season.now}, year {#year:digits}. Restricted.
  (has:company) {company}: annual report, year {#year:digits}.
  A report of the ministry, on the state of the {mr.what}.
  The {mr.what}: a report for the year {#year:digits}.
  Confidential. The state of the {mr.what} in {$home}.
  To the committee on the {mr.what}, from the inspectors.
  Survey of the {mr.what}, {$home} district, {season.now}.
  The inspectors' report on the {mr.what}, year {#year:digits}.

mr.what (people=6)
  water supply
  harvest
  roads
  population
  grid
  schools
  hospitals
  markets
  housing
  trams
  {craft} trade
  {crop} crop
  (coast=1) harbour
  (coast=1) fisheries
  (desert=0) forests
  (economy=herding|economy2=herding) herds

# ---- what the report is ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

mr.summary (share=0.8)
  This report covers {mr.span}, {mr.sum.how}.
  The inspectors visited {#n|district} and {#nbig} households, {mr.sum.ins}.
  The figures were collected {mr.sum.coll}, and some of them are {mr.sum.qual}.
  The last report {mr.last}, so this one is {mr.shorter}.
  It was asked for by {ruler.the} in {season.any}, and it is {mr.late}.
  (stage>=0) This report concerns the long-term trend, which the committee asked us not to call {mr.word}.
mr.span (people=4)
  the year
  the last {#n|year}
  the months of {season.any}
  the districts north of {$seat}
  the whole of {$home}
  the river towns
  the {craft} trade
  the {crop} harvest
mr.sum.how (people=3)
  as the committee asked
  as far as the figures allow
  with some gaps
  and is late
  at the request of {ruler.the}
  for the third time
  without the help of the ministry
  in the spirit of the founder
  with the figures the {craft} guild would release
  by hand and by lamplight
  as plainly as we can
mr.sum.ins (people=3)
  in all weathers
  on foot
  by tram
  and were welcomed in most of them
  and were given {drink} in most of them
  and counted the {herd} as well
mr.sum.coll (people=3)
  under difficult conditions
  by the schools
  by the {craft} guild
  in a hurry
  twice
mr.sum.qual (people=2)
  guesses
  old
  better than nothing
  the clerk's own
mr.last (people=4)
  was not read
  was lost
  was read and ignored
  was too long
  was answered with a letter of thanks and nothing else
  was used to light a stove
  was misfiled under {crop}
mr.shorter (people=3)
  shorter
  in plainer words
  on one page
  late
  in larger print
mr.late
  late
  shorter than was hoped
  frank
mr.word
  a crisis
  a decline
  a problem
  anything at all

# ---- what was found ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

mr.finding
  (4) {mr.thing} {mr.change} {mr.since}{mr.because}.
  (once) {mr.outof} is {n} parts in a hundred {mr.updown} the previous year{mr.forecast}.
  (once) {mr.costs} have {mr.costv} in {#n|year}{mr.because}.
  (once) The population of {mr.pop} continues to {mr.popv}{mr.because}.
  (once has:$home.quarter) {mr.share} of the houses in {$home.quarter} have no {mr.lack}.
  (once stage<0) The figures are, {mr.onwhole}, satisfactory.
  (once stage>=1) The decline is now in every district, {mr.decl}.
  (once stage>=2) We can no longer maintain the {mr.serv} to the outer towns.
mr.thing (people=10)
  Demand for water
  The number of children in the schools
  The yield of {crop} per field
  Traffic on the {bc.road}
  The cost of {fuel}
  The number of empty houses in {$home}
  Use of the hospitals
  The price of {food}
  Output of the {craft} works
  Attendance at {holyplace}
  The number of {craft} workshops
  Use of {watersrc.n} water
  The number of marriages
  Membership of the {craft} guild
  The sale of {drink}
  The number of {herd} in the district
  (coast=1) The catch of {fish}
  (has:$home.landmark) The number of visitors to {$home.landmark}
  (has:$home.quarter) Crime in {$home.quarter}
  The export of {crop2}
mr.change (people=6)
  has risen by a {nth}
  has fallen by a {nth}
  is unchanged
  has doubled
  has halved
  is at its lowest since the records began
  is at its highest in {#n|decade}
  has risen slightly
  has fallen sharply
  has gone up and down for no reason anyone can find
mr.since (people=4)
  in {#n|year}
  since the last report
  since the census
  over the decade
  {season.this}
  since the new tolls
  since {festival} last year
mr.because
  (3)
  , owing to {mr.cause}
  , which nobody can explain
  , as forecast
  , against every forecast
  , which the committee puts down to {mr.cause}
mr.cause (people=5)
  the dry {season.any}
  the cost of {fuel}
  the new road
  the closing of the {craft} works
  people leaving for {$seat}
  the price of {food}
  the old pipes
  {weather}
  (war=1) the war
  (sick=1) the sickness
mr.outof (people=3)
  Output
  Output of the {craft} works
  The {crop} harvest
  Revenue
  Attendance
  (coast=1) The catch
mr.updown
  below
  above
mr.forecast
  (2)
  , in line with the forecast
  , against the forecast
mr.costs (people=4)
  Costs
  Wages
  Prices at the market
  Rents in {$home}
  The prices of {food} and {drink}
  Fares on the {msg.transit}
  The cost of a {vessel.one.n} of {crop}
  Doctors' fees
  The price of a cart of {fuel}
mr.costv (people=3)
  doubled
  trebled
  risen by half
  fallen by a third
  crept up
  jumped
mr.pop (people=4)
  the outer towns
  the river villages
  the hill country
  the old town
  the mill streets
  the farms north of {$seat}
  the {craft} towns
  (coast=1) the coast
  (coast=1) the fishing villages
mr.popv (people=4)
  fall
  rise
  age
  drift towards {$seat}
  fall, slowly, as it has for a generation
  rise, which nobody expected
  change, and not for the better
mr.share (people=2)
  Half
  A third
  Most
  Nearly all
  A quarter
mr.lack (people=3)
  running water
  heating
  glass in the windows
  a {mod.room2}
mod.room2 (people=2)
  kitchen
  privy
  bath
  stove
mr.onwhole (people=4)
  on the whole
  for once
  in most districts
  if read kindly
  by the standards of the last decade
  in the towns, if not in the hills
  as the clerk would put it
  against all expectation
  except where they are not
mr.decl (people=2)
  the hills first
  the coast last
  as was foreseen
mr.serv (people=2)
  services
  trams
  clinics
  schools

mr.survey
  Of {#nbig} households asked, {mr.surveyres}.
  Asked what they most wanted, most of those asked in {$home} said {mr.want}.
  The survey found that {mr.surveyres}.
mr.surveyres (people=5)
  most said they had enough {food}
  a third said they would leave if they could
  nearly all said the {msg.transit} was late
  half had not heard of the committee
  most named {pastime} as their first pleasure
  a quarter had kept {herd} in the last year
  most said they trusted {ruler.the}, and most of those said it quietly
  nearly half had a relative in {$seat}
  the commonest complaint was the noise of the {craft} works
  most could name the founder of the town and few could name the mayor
mr.want (people=4)
  a new {msg.place}
  cheaper {food}
  fewer reports
  the old {festival} customs back
  a bridge
  quiet
  work
  a {msg.transit} that comes

mr.compare
  {mr.cmpa} {mr.cmpv} twice the {mr.cmpx} of {mr.cmpb}.
  {$home} spends a {nth} of its budget on {mr.spend}, {$seat} half that.
  The coastal towns and the inland towns are moving in opposite directions.
  (has:$home.quarter) {$home.quarter} has the highest rate of {mr.ill} in {$home}.
mr.cmpa (people=3)
  The northern districts
  The river towns
  The old town
  The new streets
  (coast=1) The coastal towns
mr.cmpv (people=2)
  use
  spend
  lose
  need
mr.cmpx (people=2)
  water
  {fuel}
  {food}
  money on repairs
mr.cmpb (people=2)
  the southern
  the hill towns
  the rest of {$home}
  {$seat}
mr.ill (people=3)
  sickness
  unemployment
  fires
  accidents
  theft
mr.spend (people=2)
  the roads
  the schools
  {fuel}
  the {craft} works

# ---- what is recommended -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

mr.rec
  (3) We recommend {mr.act} {mr.act2}.
  We have one recommendation: {mr.act}.
  (stage>=1) We recommend that the population be told the truth {mr.act2}.
mr.act (people=4)
  that the matter be kept under review
  that a committee be formed
  that the figures be published
  immediate action
  that the {craft} works be inspected
  that the {mr.fix} be repaired
  that {ruler.the} be told plainly
  nothing, since nothing will be done
  that the old {watersrc.n} be opened again
  a study of the study
  a tax on {drink}
  that the {herd} be moved out of the town
  that the schools teach {craft}
  a new road to {$seat}
  that the price of {food} be fixed
  that the {min.building} be closed
  that the {craft} guild be consulted
  that the old {watersrc.n} be cleaned
  a count of every {beast} in the district
  that the trams run later
  that the schools open earlier
  that the price of {fuel} be reviewed
  that the stores of {crop} be inspected
  that the report be read
  that {$home} be given its own {min.building}
  a new bridge over {river}
  that the {festival} holiday be moved
  that no further reports be commissioned
  that the inspectors be paid
  that the north road be widened
mr.act2 (people=3)
  (3)
  before {season.next}
  at once
  within the year
  , as a matter of urgency
  , for what it is worth
mr.fix (people=3)
  pipes
  roads
  bridges
  schools
  dykes
  pumps
mr.coda (share=0.6)
  We made the same recommendation {mr.same}.
  We would be glad to be {mr.glad}.
  The figures are attached{mr.att}.
  The committee thanks {mr.thanks}.
  The cost of this report is given in the appendix{mr.cost}.
  A shorter version has been sent to {ruler.the}.
  The inspectors ask that this report be read before it is filed.
mr.same (people=3)
  last year
  in the last report
  twice before
  every year since the census
  in {season.any} and in the year before
  to three governments
  in writing and by hand
mr.glad (people=3)
  wrong
  proved wrong
  contradicted
  ignored, for once
  overruled by events
  shown up by the farmers
mr.att
  (2)
  , with the gaps marked
  , in the clerk's hand
mr.thanks (people=3)
  the staff of {$home}
  the people of {$home}
  the {craft} guild
  the schoolchildren who counted
  the clerks who copied it
  the families who opened their doors
  the {herd} keepers, who were patient
  the keeper of {holyplace}
mr.cost
  (2)
  , and is not small
  , and was paid by the {craft} guild
)VG"
